<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otmuchów</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otmuchów is a small town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opole">Opole</a> Voivodeship of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nysa">Nysa</a>. With Nysa it formed the core of the territory held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wroclaw">Wrocław</a> from the 12th century, and its castle served as an episcopal residence. Like Nysa, it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1742.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otmuchow.jpg" alt="Otmuchów" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lestat (Jan Mehlich) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otmuch%C3%B3w_-_Ratusz.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
